{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:97387",
  "title": "Important: go-fdo-server security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-13 06:06:59"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-13 06:07:36"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "This package provides a server-side implementation of the FIDO Device Onboard (FDO) specification, written in Go. FDO is an open standard for the late binding of device credentials, allowing for automated and secure on-boarding of devices when they are first powered on in their final location.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* crypto/x509: Incorrect enforcement of email constraints in crypto/x509 (CVE-2026-27137)\n\n* net/url: Incorrect parsing of IPv6 host literals in net/url (CVE-2026-25679)\n\n* net: golang: Go net package: Denial of Service via long CNAME response in LookupCNAME (CVE-2026-33811)\n\n* encoding/xml: golang: Go: Denial of Service via XML decoding recursion depth issue (CVE-2026-56859)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nAdditional Changes:\n\nFor detailed information on changes in this release, see the Rocky Linux 10 Release Notes linked from the References section.",
